{
  "$comment": "DualShock 3 operator mapping, read by the runtime (r3x-pad controls) and the panel's controller overlay. Layers: hold (or double-tap to latch) L1, R1 and R2 in any combination; the layer settles after chord_grace_s. Latching an arm layer (double-tap L1, R1 or both) is crane mode: both sticks drive the arm at a speed and it stays where left (r3x-pad controls.rs). Fixed in every layer: right stick = head, L2 = talk (hold), L3 click = pin/unpin the arm the left stick drives (base: nothing), R3 click = look at guests on/off, L3+R3 = reset everything, Start = freeze, Select tap = cancel, Select hold = menu, PS hold = motors on/off. Face order: cross, circle, square, triangle; d-pad order: up, right, down, left. A binding is {label, play|sfx|emote|act|ctl}; see PadBinding. A button whose tap is a held control (grip) has no hold binding.",
